One object can be related to multiple objects using a dependency relationship. In OOP, this
type of relationship is very common.
Let's look at another example of dependency relationships. A relationship between a
Programmer and a Computer could be a dependency relationship. How? Well, we know
that a Programmer is most likely a human and a Computer is a machine. A Programmer
uses a Computer to write computer programs, but the Computer is not a property of the
Programmer. A Programmer uses a computer, and this doesn't have to be one specific
computer — it can be any computer. So can we say that a relationship between a
Programmer and a Computer is a type of dependency relationship? Yes, we surely can.
