Composition
A composition relationship is a type of association relationship. This means that one object

will have another object as its property, but where it differs from aggregation is that, in
composition, the object that is used as a property can't exist independently; it must have the
help of another object in order to be functional. If we think about the Chef and
Manufacturer classes, the existence of these classes is not fully dependent on
the Food and Beverage classes. Instead, these classes can exist independently, and
therefore have an aggregation relationship.
